---The plugin module allows users to access and query properties for the current plugin, as well as access plugin
---resources.
---@class Plugin
Plugin = {}

---Checks if the user has allowed the specified permission for the current plugin.
---
---Info: Unless your plugin won't work at all without a specific permission, prefer marking permissions as optional in
---the manifest and using `HasPermission` to check whether or not to enable functionality that depends on that
---permission.
---@param permission PluginPermissions The permission to check.
---@return boolean # True if the specified permission has been given to this plugin, false otherwise.
function Plugin.HasPermission(permission) end

---Custom resources provided by plugins can be used as a alternative for built-in ones in various methods, but also
---provide some additional functionality.
---
---Resources are automatically loaded on demand, or can be loaded explicitly by plugins, which can be useful when
---dealing with larger resources, or to keep audio in memory to avoid any delays.
---
---See here on information on how to access the resources provided by a plugin.
---
---Info: Support for custom resources is currently limited to the following types and their associated formats:
---
---Warning: Once loaded, a resource will remain loaded until either the plugin that owns it is unloaded and all
---references to it are freed, or until the user manually unloads it.
---
---Warning: Image resources are limited to a maximum size of 1024x1024 pixels currently.
---@class PluginResource
---@field path string (Read-only) The disk path to this resource.
---@field loaded boolean (Read-only) Whether the resource's data is currently loaded and ready to use.
---@field inUse boolean (Read-only) Whether or not the resource is being used anywhere currently.
local PluginResource = {}

---Attempts to load this resource, making it ready for immediate use afterwards if successful.
---@return PluginResourceLoadResult # Indicates whether loading succeeded, or the error in case it failed.
function PluginResource:Load() end

---Attempts to unload this resource's data.
---
---No data is actually freed until all references to it have been released, meaning that if it's being used for a sprite
---elsewhere, that sprite will remain valid until it is removed as well, even though the resource itself has been
---unloaded.
function PluginResource:Unload() end

---Contains all permissions a plugin may request.
---
---In the client: Each value is a userdata of its own, not a number.
---@class PluginPermissions
---@field httpAccess PluginPermissions Allows the use of HTTP-related functionality if provided. Makes use of base URLs specified in the plugin's manifest file.
---@field chatAccess PluginPermissions Allows the use of Chat-related functionality if provided.
---@field trackingAccess PluginPermissions Allows the use of Tracking ID-related functionality if provided.
PluginPermissions = {}

---@enum PluginResourceLoadResult
PluginResourceLoadResult = {
    ---The resource has been loaded successfully.
    SUCCESS = 0,
    ---Failed to read the resource from disk.
    ERROR_FILESYSTEM = 1,
    ---Failed to decode the resource, it may be using an unsupported format.
    ERROR_DECODE = 2,
    ---Failed to load the resource as it exceeds limits.
    ERROR_EXCEEDS_LIMITS = 3,
    ---Failed to construct this resource even though loading succeeded. This can occur when attempting to load a resource during shutdown for example.
    ERROR_CONSTRUCTION = 4,
}

---The name of one of the values, as `PluginResourceLoadResult.FromID(PluginResourceLoadResult.SUCCESS)` is `"SUCCESS"`.
---@param value integer
---@return string
---@diagnostic disable-next-line: inject-field
function PluginResourceLoadResult.FromID(value) end
